+#### Per-episode prompt schedule
+
+Use a CSV file to change the policy's language prompt between episodes without
+reloading its weights. The only required column is `Prompt`; the default
+optional metadata columns are `Episode Number`, `Task Being Assessed`,
+`Condition`, and `Scene Description`.
+
+```bash
+lerobot-rollout \
+    --strategy.type=episodic \
+    --strategy.prompt_file=/path/to/evaluation_checklist.csv \
+    --strategy.start_row=0 \
+    --strategy.num_rows=110 \
+    --policy.path=${HF_USER}/my_policy \
+    --robot.type=so100_follower \
+    --robot.port=/dev/ttyACM0 \
+    --dataset.repo_id=${HF_USER}/rollout_scheduled_eval \
+    --dataset.num_episodes=110
+```
+
+`start_row` counts CSV data rows, excluding the header. When a prompt schedule
+is active, `dataset.num_episodes` is the target total dataset size. A discarded
+episode reuses the same prompt; a resumed dataset continues at the next
+unsaved prompt. Keep the same schedule slice and target size when resuming.
+
